1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,340
The second attempt began in January with a slim brochure and a wide table.

2
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:12,002
There were six copies of the manual, a dozen notebooks, and a mug that said “read me twice”.

3
00:00:12,002 --> 00:00:16,575
“So this is the semester of paper,” Maya said.

4
00:00:16,575 --> 00:00:21,963
“However, a good handbook is not a bestseller.”

5
00:00:21,963 --> 00:00:30,844
Both of them collected citations the way other people collect stamps, rather than the way examiners collect mistakes.

6
00:00:30,844 --> 00:00:41,279
A quarterly commentary, a monthly dictionary supplement, a weekly song sheet, and a yearly report were piled above the desk.

7
00:00:41,279 --> 00:00:44,647
“Cite the page,” Lin said.

8
00:00:44,647 --> 00:00:46,612
“Quote the line.

9
00:00:46,612 --> 00:00:59,481
Otherwise the reader cannot check us.” The preface of the slim volume was written last, and an additional dozen copies were ordered before anyone had read it.

10
00:00:59,481 --> 00:01:04,538
He taught a short course on the introduction of numbers into prose.

11
00:01:04,538 --> 00:01:13,100
Experience, he said, is not information; a battalion of facts can hide a single mistake.

12
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:28,303
A coal fire kept the winter evening warm, a jacket hung on the back of a chair, and a bible lay open at a genealogy: all made the same point — the staff usually remember what they can picture.

13
00:01:28,303 --> 00:01:34,910
They sought a dual method: one page for the reader, one page for oneself.

14
00:01:34,910 --> 00:01:43,685
A commentary in the margin, a datum in the corner, and a second commentary on the commentary kept them honest.

15
00:01:43,685 --> 00:01:49,373
The art of it was restraint, and the education faculty noticed.

16
00:01:49,373 --> 00:01:58,754
A monthly review of their own pages, written in pencil, became the habit that held the whole project together.

17
00:01:58,754 --> 00:02:05,691
Twelve thousand words later, the department could learn from the mistakes of the first edition.

18
00:02:05,691 --> 00:02:13,047
Twenty pages in, nine of them had to be rewritten; he did not mention it to the others.

19
00:02:13,047 --> 00:02:18,590
Sometimes they remembered the old wording; mostly they did not.

20
00:02:18,590 --> 00:02:30,810
“Seek the sort of sentence that can survive being read aloud,” she said, and so they did, in the school library, with the first snow of the year on the roof.

21
00:02:30,810 --> 00:02:34,693
Above the shelves a lamp burned all afternoon.

22
00:02:34,693 --> 00:02:45,006
The second attempt was not a correction of the first; it was a different book with the same subject, and both of them knew it.
